{"name":"Mint Circle","hex":"#a9ceaa","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mint","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A building or institution where money (originally, only coins) is produced under government licence.","A vast sum of money;  a large amount of something."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To reproduce (coins), usually en masse, under licence.","To invent; to forge; to fabricate; to fashion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mint"},{"term":"circle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A two-dimensional geometric figure, a line, consisting of the set of all those points in a plane that are equally distant from a given point (center).","A two-dimensional geometric figure, a disk, consisting of the set of all those points of a plane at a distance less than or equal to a fixed distance (radius) from a given point."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To travel around along a curved path; to orbit.","To surround; to encompass within a circle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mint (newspaper)","blocks":[{"text":"Mint is an Indian business and financial daily newspaper published by HT Media, a Delhi-based media group which is controlled by the K. K. Birla family. The family also publishes Hindustan Times. Mint was launched in 2007 and specializes in business and politics."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8c/Mint_cover_03-28-10.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mint_(newspaper)","wikidata":"Q2271133"},{"title":"Circle","blocks":[{"text":"A circle is a shape consisting of all points in a plane that are at a given distance from a given point, the centre. The distance between any point of the circle and the centre is called the radius. The length of a line segment connecting two points on the circle and passing through the centre is called the diameter. A circle bounds a region of the plane called a disc."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Circle-withsegments.svg/330px-Circle-withsegments.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circle","wikidata":"Q17278"},{"title":"Spring green","blocks":[{"text":"Spring green is a color that was traditionally considered to be on the yellow side of green, but in modern computer systems based on the RGB color model is halfway between cyan and green on the color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/%D0%97%D2%AF%D0%BC%D1%96%D1%80%D0%B5%D1%82.jpg/330px-%D0%97%D2%AF%D0%BC%D1%96%D1%80%D0%B5%D1%82.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_green","wikidata":"Q373787"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/2009_07_09_camino_cielo_paradise_137.jpg/500px-2009_07_09_camino_cielo_paradise_137.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/2009_07_09_camino_cielo_paradise_137.jpg/1280px-2009_07_09_camino_cielo_paradise_137.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/2009_07_09_camino_cielo_paradise_137.jpg/500px-2009_07_09_camino_cielo_paradise_137.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Circular cave paintings in Santa Barbara County, California","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2009_07_09_camino_cielo_paradise_137.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Shatir500.jpg/330px-Shatir500.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Shatir500.jpg/330px-Shatir500.jpg?utm_source=en